WEBVTT

00:01.700 --> 00:05.177
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:05.178 --> 00:08.486
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.537 --> 00:11.962
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:12.030 --> 00:14.921
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:15.006 --> 00:18.549
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:18.600 --> 00:21.741
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.808 --> 00:22.977
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:23.046 --> 00:24.298
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.366 --> 00:26.572
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:35.894 --> 00:37.160
All right, see
you guys later.

00:37.161 --> 00:38.881
Me and Brian are
going to play laser tag

00:38.949 --> 00:39.901
with Joe and Quagmire.

00:39.969 --> 00:41.155
What?! No, you're not.

00:41.223 --> 00:42.726
Tonight's our family night.

00:42.794 --> 00:44.965
We agreed that every Sunday,
we'd do something together.

00:45.033 --> 00:46.236
(clears throat)

00:46.304 --> 00:47.439
What?

00:47.507 --> 00:49.078
Oh, nothing. I was just
clearing my throat.

00:49.146 --> 00:50.950
Good. I thought you were
going to say something.

00:51.017 --> 00:52.772
But, Lois, we
already made plans.

00:52.840 --> 00:54.293
Yeah, I can't leave
those guys alone.

00:54.361 --> 00:56.532
Last time they hung out
without me was a disaster.

00:56.601 --> 00:58.371
All right, movie night.

00:58.439 --> 01:00.845
<i>I am so psyched
for Reindeer Games!</i>

01:00.913 --> 01:03.085
<i>What, I thought we
were watching La Vie En Rose.</i>

01:03.153 --> 01:05.108
<i>What do you mean,
Reindeer Games is great!</i>

01:05.176 --> 01:08.250
Everything goes wrong on the one
day it has to go right.

01:08.318 --> 01:10.088
<i>But La Vie En Rose
is a beautiful movie</i>

01:10.157 --> 01:12.362
about the real life tragedy
of Edith Piaf.

01:12.430 --> 01:13.950
Usually Peter would
break the tie.

01:14.018 --> 01:15.338
Well, Peter
isn't here, is he?!

01:15.405 --> 01:17.076
Because you were
supposed to be watching him,

01:17.144 --> 01:19.249
but you were smoking
marijuana and he drowned!

01:19.316 --> 01:21.221
What? No, he's at
a PTA meeting.

01:21.289 --> 01:23.009
Where the hell
did you get that story?

01:23.077 --> 01:25.517
I don't know! I just can't stand
it when he's not here!

01:25.585 --> 01:27.273
Peter, you've got
every other night of the week

01:27.340 --> 01:28.643
to spend with your buddies.

01:28.711 --> 01:31.217
This is the one night
we've set aside for our family.

01:31.285 --> 01:33.088
Is that really
too much to ask?

01:33.156 --> 01:34.626
(sighs)
I guess you're right.

01:34.677 --> 01:36.181
Come on, Brian.
Come upstairs.

01:36.266 --> 01:38.806
I wanna show you a freckle on my
sack that I'm concerned about.

01:38.874 --> 01:40.026
It has irregular edges.

01:41.598 --> 01:42.403
(window opening)

01:42.428 --> 01:43.731
BRIAN (whispers): Peter,
what are you doing?

01:43.804 --> 01:45.173
PETER (whispers):
I'm not goin' to Family Night.

01:45.242 --> 01:47.381
My agreeing with Lois
was just pure theater.

01:47.448 --> 01:48.818
Come on, we're
jumping off the roof.

01:48.886 --> 01:50.390
Are you insane?!
We'll kill ourselves!

01:50.457 --> 01:51.761
Don't worry, we can fly.

01:51.828 --> 01:53.800
I got this pixie dust
from a magic fairy.

01:53.868 --> 01:55.169
Either that or it's speed

01:55.238 --> 01:56.941
I got from a transvestite
at a diner.

01:57.009 --> 01:59.048
(snorting)

01:59.115 --> 02:01.220
(yells): It's the speed!
It's the speed from the diner!

02:01.289 --> 02:02.491
Peter, let go of me!

02:02.559 --> 02:04.079
(yells)
Damn it!

02:06.235 --> 02:08.375
So what are we gonna do
for Family Night?

02:08.443 --> 02:11.016
Oh, would you shut up?
All the good people are gone.

02:14.661 --> 02:18.136
Hey!
Welcome to Quahog Laser Tag.

02:18.204 --> 02:20.109
Please pay attention
while I show y'all

02:20.176 --> 02:21.881
how to put on y'all's vests.

02:21.949 --> 02:23.586
Sir, can I use you
to demonstrate?

02:23.653 --> 02:25.860
Thank you, I have
longed for your attention

02:25.927 --> 02:27.664
since the moment I arrived.

02:27.732 --> 02:30.104
Now, put this on
over your shoulders.

02:30.172 --> 02:31.408
Good.

02:31.476 --> 02:33.080
Now, I'm gonna need
you to squats down

02:33.148 --> 02:34.584
like your underwears
is done for,

02:34.652 --> 02:36.423
but you might still
save the jeans.

02:39.817 --> 02:42.808
Now, you's gonna wanna latch the
front to the back like so...

02:42.876 --> 02:44.547
Did everybody get that?

02:44.614 --> 02:47.104
Boy, a lot of heat
comes off you, don't it?

02:47.171 --> 02:50.197
(lasers zapping)

02:50.281 --> 02:52.621
All right, keep an
eye out for Peter.

02:52.688 --> 02:55.695
He's oddly competitive
at this stuff.

02:55.746 --> 02:59.424
Yeah, and he seems to be weirdly
physically fit at this place.

02:59.508 --> 03:01.095
Yeah, it's almost like he has

03:01.179 --> 03:03.519
unrealistic abilities
when we play laser tag.

03:05.692 --> 03:08.165
All right, well, if we just
stick together, then...

03:08.232 --> 03:09.285
Zap! Zap! Zap!

03:09.369 --> 03:10.371
What the...
No way!

03:10.423 --> 03:11.391
How'd you learn
to do that?

03:11.460 --> 03:13.397
The question isn't how I do it.

03:13.466 --> 03:16.840
It's how I forgive myself
for what I've done.

03:16.908 --> 03:18.211
(zap)

03:18.279 --> 03:20.535
Yeah, winner!
Right here!

03:20.602 --> 03:22.039
All right, pal,
what do I get?

03:22.107 --> 03:23.911
Well, for five dollars,
you could get

03:23.980 --> 03:26.486
your picture in a fake newspaper
with a humorous headline.

03:29.260 --> 03:31.165
Wow, my picture
in the paper.

03:31.233 --> 03:32.770
I didn't even
get that when

03:32.838 --> 03:34.509
I brought that kitten
and gorilla together.

03:34.577 --> 03:36.749
Huh?
Did I tell ya, Lois?

03:36.816 --> 03:38.821
Oh, that's beautiful, Peter.

03:38.889 --> 03:41.496
She's taking care of that
kitten like it's her own.

03:41.563 --> 03:44.003
Yep, I knew eventually she'd
stop tearin' 'em in half.

03:48.684 --> 03:50.338
There you two are!

03:50.406 --> 03:52.211
We waited for you
for four hours!

03:52.277 --> 03:53.413
Where the hell
have you been?!

03:53.481 --> 03:54.967
Look, Lois,
I know you're mad,

03:55.036 --> 03:57.374
but I think this will prove
that I did the right thing.

03:57.426 --> 04:00.250
I put our family
on the map tonight.

04:00.318 --> 04:03.226
No longer will we be
just those faceless nobodies

04:03.294 --> 04:04.863
who brought the bird flu
to Quahog.

04:04.931 --> 04:07.002
You know, there's something
seriously wrong with a man

04:07.071 --> 04:09.042
who always puts
his friends over his family.

04:09.094 --> 04:10.764
Come on, Lois, I think
you're overreacting.

04:10.832 --> 04:13.138
What's so wrong about a guy
hanging out with his buddies?

04:13.223 --> 04:15.278
Buddies?
You're one of his buddies?

04:15.362 --> 04:16.413
Yeah. And you know why?

04:16.481 --> 04:17.584
'Cause I don't try to tell him

04:17.652 --> 04:18.620
what he can and can't do.

04:18.688 --> 04:20.325
Oh, please, Brian.

04:20.393 --> 04:22.649
You're just two people
who live in the same house.

04:22.717 --> 04:24.154
If you didn't,
you'd never hang out

04:24.221 --> 04:25.725
with each other
in a million years.

04:25.793 --> 04:27.863
He owns you.
You're his property.

04:27.931 --> 04:29.601
He used to hang you
in the garage

04:29.670 --> 04:31.340
so his fender
wouldn't hit the wall.

04:31.408 --> 04:34.466
(music playing over radio)
You're there.

04:34.534 --> 04:36.472
You're there!

04:36.540 --> 04:38.612
I couldn't hear you.
The radio was too loud.

04:41.420 --> 04:43.642
I'm going to bed.

04:43.694 --> 04:45.365
You know,
Lois is right, Brian.

04:45.432 --> 04:47.387
You think you're Peter's pal,
but you're really not.

04:47.455 --> 04:49.042
You're just his dog.

04:49.110 --> 04:50.948
Well, that's where
you're wrong. Watch this.

04:51.016 --> 04:52.753
Hey, Peter, you want
to go hit the Clam?

04:52.837 --> 04:54.391
Nah, there's no way
she's in the mood.

04:54.475 --> 04:56.263
Let's just go to the bar.
Sounds good.

04:56.348 --> 04:58.720
Headin' to the bar
with my friend, Peter.

04:58.772 --> 05:00.107
You're lying
to yourself, Brian.

05:00.175 --> 05:01.713
Like those girls who insist

05:01.781 --> 05:03.483
their best friends
are attractive.

05:03.551 --> 05:06.124
Oh, Stewie, I can't wait for
you to meet my best friend.

05:06.192 --> 05:07.395
She is so cute.

05:07.463 --> 05:08.866
Yeah, she sounds awesome.

05:08.934 --> 05:10.638
Oh, my God, yeah.
People ask her

05:10.706 --> 05:12.142
if she's a model
all the time.

05:12.210 --> 05:13.798
Here she comes!

05:13.866 --> 05:16.638
(chuckles)
Okay, okay,

05:16.706 --> 05:18.009
that was an extreme example,

05:18.077 --> 05:21.052
but face it, ladies,
your best friends are not hot.

05:25.181 --> 05:27.938
Uh, Peter, your seat belt
back here doesn't work right.

05:27.989 --> 05:30.028
What's gonna happen to you
that hasn't already happened?

05:30.112 --> 05:31.415
Peter, look out
for that car!

05:31.483 --> 05:33.170
(high-pitched tone resonates)

05:33.254 --> 05:34.291
That's not a car.

05:34.342 --> 05:35.511
What is that?!

05:35.595 --> 05:37.467
(all screaming)

05:49.553 --> 05:51.925
Hello?

05:54.800 --> 05:56.638
Hello?

05:57.776 --> 05:59.079
Anybody here?

06:03.024 --> 06:04.127
Hey.

06:04.194 --> 06:05.564
Hey.

06:05.632 --> 06:06.919
Do you work here?

06:06.986 --> 06:09.242
I don't know.
Doesn't look like it.

06:09.309 --> 06:10.729
Who are you?

06:10.797 --> 06:13.655
I... I don't know.
I-I just woke up here.

06:13.723 --> 06:15.727
I seem to be
a heavyset fellow.

06:15.795 --> 06:17.950
You do.

06:18.002 --> 06:19.572
Thank God someone
else is here.

06:19.640 --> 06:21.812
You two seem to be the only
ones in this hospital.

06:21.897 --> 06:23.400
No, I'm here, too.

06:23.468 --> 06:25.305
Any of you guys
know what's going on?

06:25.373 --> 06:27.445
I just woke up in
one of these rooms.

06:27.513 --> 06:29.584
I have no idea
how I got here.

06:29.652 --> 06:31.423
I don't even
know who I am.

06:31.491 --> 06:34.432
All I know is,
I'm extremely important

06:34.500 --> 06:36.739
because there are drawings of me
on all the bathroom doors.

06:36.806 --> 06:38.494
See?

06:38.561 --> 06:41.836
It's glued on there, too, so I'm
pretty sure it's permanent.

06:41.904 --> 06:43.107
This is really weird.

06:43.175 --> 06:44.912
We seem perfectly coherent,

06:44.981 --> 06:46.751
it's just we can't
remember who we are.

06:46.819 --> 06:48.657
It's like our identities
have been

06:48.725 --> 06:49.994
wiped out somehow.

06:50.061 --> 06:51.732
Maybe we can find somebody
to help us.

07:02.363 --> 07:04.168
(dial tone droning)

07:04.236 --> 07:06.842
The whole town seems
to be deserted.

07:06.910 --> 07:08.548
Well, if there are
only four of us,

07:08.616 --> 07:10.086
I propose we start a band.

07:10.154 --> 07:13.011
And I propose we call
ourselves Robes of Teal.

07:13.079 --> 07:14.649
Aw, damn it.

07:17.023 --> 07:19.630
Well, we could still be a band
and choose a different name.

07:19.681 --> 07:21.402
Oh, no, Robes of Teal
was the whole thing.

07:38.178 --> 07:39.548
What the hell happened?
Where is everybody?

07:40.065 --> 07:41.368
You don't suppose...

07:41.436 --> 07:43.558
Do you think, we're the
only people on Earth?

07:43.626 --> 07:45.163
I don't know.
I tell ya what,

07:45.214 --> 07:47.269
I'm gonna open up
this bag of Chex Party Mix.

07:47.337 --> 07:48.873
If people don't show up,
then we're it.

07:50.646 --> 07:52.517
Yep, we're it.

07:52.585 --> 07:55.091
All right, look, we know
we woke up in the hospital,

07:55.160 --> 07:57.265
so maybe there was some kind
of catastrophe

07:57.333 --> 07:58.703
that we were all spared.

07:58.770 --> 08:00.875
Or maybe we were all
in some kind of accident.

08:00.942 --> 08:02.914
Well, that would explain
why you're in a wheelchair.

08:02.982 --> 08:04.987
You must have gotten hurt
worse than the rest of us.

08:05.054 --> 08:07.611
Yeah, I got hit so hard,
it knocked my pee into a bag.

08:07.680 --> 08:08.949
None of this
makes any sense.

08:09.016 --> 08:10.118
Where the hell
is everybody?

08:10.204 --> 08:11.807
Well, if we wait
till tax day,

08:11.875 --> 08:13.344
I'm sure the tax man
will show up.

08:13.412 --> 08:14.715
Ha. You should tweet that.

08:14.766 --> 08:17.256
Okay.

08:17.324 --> 08:18.560
(cell phone buzzes)

08:18.627 --> 08:19.964
(laughs)
This guy's hilarious.

08:20.032 --> 08:21.435
I'm gonna retweet this.

08:21.503 --> 08:22.973
(both cell phones buzz)

08:23.041 --> 08:24.376
Huh.
Mm.

08:24.444 --> 08:27.151
Social media is bringing us
all closer together.

08:27.219 --> 08:28.355
Unfollow.

08:30.930 --> 08:32.617
Hey, you know,
if we're all gonna be

08:32.685 --> 08:34.088
tryin' to figure
this out together,

08:34.156 --> 08:36.311
maybe it would be easier
if we gave each other names.

08:36.362 --> 08:37.665
That's a great idea.

08:37.750 --> 08:39.838
Hey, maybe my name
is on this collar.

08:39.923 --> 08:42.211
Cremate, don't bury.

08:42.297 --> 08:43.332
Okay, that's a downer.

08:43.383 --> 08:44.669
You know what?

08:44.720 --> 08:46.608
I'm gettin' a feeling
about my name.

08:46.676 --> 08:49.449
I think my name
might be Shirt Pants.

08:49.517 --> 08:51.572
Shirt Pants?
What kind of name is that?

08:51.657 --> 08:52.859
I don't know.
What's your name?

08:52.911 --> 08:54.748
I kinda think
it's Manly Walker.

08:54.833 --> 08:56.370
Wheeler?
No, Walker.

08:56.421 --> 08:57.724
Wheeler?
No, you're not hearing me right.

08:57.809 --> 08:58.844
It's Walker.

08:58.895 --> 09:00.047
It's probably Wheeler.

09:00.114 --> 09:01.685
I sorta think
my name is Earl.

09:01.736 --> 09:03.574
<i>(My Name is Earl theme plays)</i>

09:03.658 --> 09:05.028
What was that?
I don't know.

09:05.079 --> 09:06.750
Apparently, I made
some sort of reference.

09:06.835 --> 09:09.625
Hey, check it out.
Looks like a bar.

09:09.693 --> 09:11.398
(sighs) I could go
for a stiff one.

09:11.464 --> 09:12.968
I think they got
a pill for that.

09:13.036 --> 09:14.238
Shirt Pants!

09:14.305 --> 09:17.080
Who else but Shirt Pants?

09:17.148 --> 09:19.721
♪ He's Shirt Pants,
Shirt Pants ♪

09:19.789 --> 09:21.995
♪ She's tryin' to remember,
but he really can't ♪

09:22.063 --> 09:24.100
♪ He's Shirt Pants,
Shirt Pants ♪

09:24.168 --> 09:27.025
♪ All I know for sure is I'm
wearing a shirt and pants. ♪

09:28.146 --> 09:29.750
Hello?

09:29.818 --> 09:32.091
♪ A-well-a everybody's heard
about the bird ♪

09:32.158 --> 09:34.865
♪ B-B-Bird, bird, bird,
b-bird's the word... ♪

09:34.934 --> 09:36.870
That's annoying.

09:36.955 --> 09:38.659
BRIAN:
It just doesn't make sense

09:38.710 --> 09:39.930
that there aren't any people.

09:39.997 --> 09:41.668
This couldn't have
happened naturally.

09:41.719 --> 09:44.527
Something must have
caused this, or someone.

09:44.595 --> 09:47.585
Well, when I find that person,
I'm gonna strangle him.

09:47.653 --> 09:50.226
I had a life,
and he took it away from me.

09:50.294 --> 09:52.717
I don't remember it,
but I bet it was pretty good.

09:52.784 --> 09:54.088
Yeah, me, too.

09:54.156 --> 09:55.960
I bet I was a doctor
who had to deal with

09:56.028 --> 09:57.865
a lot of serious stuff,
but always found a way

09:57.934 --> 09:58.968
to keep things light.

10:00.206 --> 10:02.411
Oh, my God,
she's beautiful.

10:02.480 --> 10:03.849
Yeah, she is.

10:03.917 --> 10:06.591
It's not yours.
Yours died.

10:06.675 --> 10:08.129
Yeah, and I bet I answered

10:08.197 --> 10:10.435
the customer complaint line
at a Danish cookie company.

10:10.504 --> 10:13.210
Hello, Danish cookie company.

10:13.277 --> 10:16.219
No, I know they don't
taste very good.

10:16.286 --> 10:18.458
Well, because
they're very dry, aren't they?

10:18.527 --> 10:19.997
I mean, t-they came in a tin,

10:20.065 --> 10:22.103
how fresh did you think
they were gonna be?

10:22.171 --> 10:24.342
Look, it's dark
and freezing in Denmark.

10:24.409 --> 10:26.716
Everybody who made these cookies
has shot themselves.

10:26.783 --> 10:29.508
Well, I bet I did something
really important and exciting.

10:29.575 --> 10:31.313
Like-like maybe I was
a speechwriter

10:31.380 --> 10:32.951
for the first ever
black president.

10:34.890 --> 10:36.493
Hey, can he say
the word "ask"?

10:36.562 --> 10:38.433
Or-or is that a word
we should avoid?

10:38.500 --> 10:41.710
Yea, and I bet you I was the
voice of an animated bird.

10:41.777 --> 10:44.351
(Joe's voice):
I thought I saw a cat.

10:44.418 --> 10:46.924
I did see a cat.

10:46.992 --> 10:48.963
Oh, my God,
look at that.

10:51.472 --> 10:53.210
Wow, that looks
pretty bad.

10:53.277 --> 10:54.513
Is the Chinese
guy dead?

10:54.582 --> 10:55.650
(sniffs)
Wait.

10:55.718 --> 10:58.207
(sniffs)
We-we were in this car.

10:58.275 --> 10:59.812
I can smell us all
in this car!

10:59.879 --> 11:01.450
This must be the accident

11:01.517 --> 11:03.089
that put us all
in the hospital.

11:03.156 --> 11:05.378
See if there's a registration
in the glove compartment.

11:08.188 --> 11:09.690
"Peter Griffin."

11:09.758 --> 11:11.562
One of us is Peter Griffin.

11:11.631 --> 11:13.451
Look at this indent
on the steering wheel.

11:15.860 --> 11:16.895
It's a perfect match.

11:16.963 --> 11:17.931
Oh, my God!

11:17.999 --> 11:19.051
You're Peter Griffin!

11:19.119 --> 11:20.355
Yeah, I am.

11:20.423 --> 11:22.360
And you live
at 31 Spooner Street.

11:22.428 --> 11:24.099
Finally, a real clue.
Let's go!

11:24.167 --> 11:25.636
Wow, I own a house!

11:25.705 --> 11:26.941
I just hope it doesn't have

11:27.008 --> 11:28.947
one of those mailboxes
that looks like a cow.

11:29.014 --> 11:31.989
<i>I just want to seem cool to
these guys, but I really hope</i>

11:32.057 --> 11:34.529
<i>I have one of those mailboxes
that looks like a cow.</i>

11:34.597 --> 11:36.769
<i>"Moo," says my mailbox.</i>

11:39.846 --> 11:41.115
Well, this is
31 Spooner Street.

11:41.184 --> 11:42.353
I'm home.

11:42.420 --> 11:43.623
All right,
see you guys.

11:43.691 --> 11:45.060
I'm gonna go shove my
hand down my pants

11:45.127 --> 11:46.197
and see if that
goes someplace.

11:49.072 --> 11:51.780
Guys! Guys!
It goes someplace!

11:51.848 --> 11:54.338
(sniffs)
Hang on, I got something.

11:54.405 --> 11:57.144
(sniffing)

11:57.212 --> 11:59.635
I poop a lot on this lawn.

11:59.703 --> 12:01.073
This must be where I live!

12:02.595 --> 12:03.899
Hey, Shirt Pants,
come in here.

12:05.738 --> 12:07.309
Oh, my God!

12:07.377 --> 12:08.862
I know, I know!
You're my owner!

12:08.930 --> 12:10.484
I knew it!
I knew we were pals!

12:10.568 --> 12:12.290
Yeah, I mean, there's
no pictures of me,

12:12.374 --> 12:14.296
but I see you've got a
dog collar and a leash.

12:14.363 --> 12:16.217
And look how big
your doggie cage is.

12:16.286 --> 12:17.455
You could fit
a human in there.

12:17.522 --> 12:18.993
Clearly, you're
a good owner.

12:21.567 --> 12:23.237
It's such a
weird situation.

12:23.306 --> 12:25.344
I-I just think somebody
should be writing about it.

12:25.412 --> 12:26.614
Yeah.

12:26.665 --> 12:28.453
Do you... do you think
it should be me?

12:28.521 --> 12:30.509
S-Should I be the one
writing about this?

12:30.594 --> 12:31.662
Uh, I don't know.

12:31.714 --> 12:33.266
I-I think it
should be me.

12:33.335 --> 12:35.440
Then just do it, stop talking
about it for God's sake.

12:36.711 --> 12:38.281
Oh, hey, guys.

12:38.350 --> 12:39.719
Well, we got it
all figured out.

12:39.787 --> 12:41.558
Turns out my name
is Glenn Quagmire,

12:41.626 --> 12:42.811
and this is my dog.

12:42.880 --> 12:44.099
JOE:
Hey, you guys!

12:44.167 --> 12:45.335
Hey, I found my house.

12:45.403 --> 12:47.007
Turns out my name's
Joe Swanson,

12:47.075 --> 12:49.213
and I found this
police uniform in my closet.

12:49.281 --> 12:50.517
Do you know
what that means?

12:50.585 --> 12:51.771
I'm a stripper!

12:53.243 --> 12:55.281
Well, it's good
we found out who we all are,

12:55.349 --> 12:56.618
but we still
haven't found out

12:56.702 --> 12:58.356
what the hell happened
to everybody else.

12:58.425 --> 12:59.827
Yeah, I've been
thinking about that,

12:59.896 --> 13:01.633
and I think the
best course of action

13:01.701 --> 13:04.525
is for us to just go ahead and
start repopulating the Earth.

13:04.593 --> 13:05.996
But there are no women.

13:06.064 --> 13:07.233
Well, let's try
some stuff.

13:07.284 --> 13:09.021
Hey, you guys want to
see something cool?

13:09.089 --> 13:11.428
There's a bedroom upstairs
that belonged to some girl,

13:11.496 --> 13:12.966
and she's got bras in there,

13:13.034 --> 13:14.671
and the cups are
different sizes.

13:14.739 --> 13:16.477
L-Like one of them's
a martini glass

13:16.544 --> 13:17.813
and the other one's
some kinda melon.

13:21.140 --> 13:23.229
Guys, you know how
we were thinking

13:23.296 --> 13:25.703
that something must have
caused this situation...

13:25.771 --> 13:27.141
or someone?
Yeah?

13:27.208 --> 13:28.980
Look at that.

13:34.061 --> 13:35.197
Oh, my God.

13:35.281 --> 13:36.183
It's him.

13:36.251 --> 13:37.286
He did this.

13:37.354 --> 13:38.323
What do we do?

13:38.390 --> 13:39.560
Check it out.

13:39.628 --> 13:40.830
I got the little
freak's bra.

13:40.898 --> 13:42.051
I'm gonna put it on.

13:43.856 --> 13:45.894
Huh, this actually
fits pretty well.

13:45.962 --> 13:47.533
Oh, wait, there's
a name on it.

13:48.515 --> 13:49.717
It's mine.

13:55.153 --> 13:56.556
My God.

13:56.624 --> 13:58.946
Peter is responsible for
killing everyone on Earth.

13:59.014 --> 14:01.638
But how could a guy like that
cause all this destruction?

14:01.706 --> 14:03.844
Well, he's clearly
not just a guy.

14:03.912 --> 14:06.017
He's some kind of
omnipotent alien,

14:06.086 --> 14:07.888
with powers we can
only guess at.

14:07.956 --> 14:09.861
Look at him--
watching, learning...

14:09.929 --> 14:11.567
absorbing.

14:11.635 --> 14:14.174
This janitor's in love
with this redheaded ashtray.

14:17.753 --> 14:19.255
But why didn't
he kill us?

14:19.323 --> 14:21.361
I don't know, maybe...
maybe he needs us.

14:21.429 --> 14:22.832
Maybe we're important.

14:22.900 --> 14:25.641
I mean, I do have all these
profound ideas and thoughts.

14:25.709 --> 14:27.112
Maybe I was a deep
thinker of some kind.

14:27.180 --> 14:28.249
Deep thinker?

14:28.317 --> 14:29.452
I spent the whole morning

14:29.520 --> 14:31.089
trying to teach you
one simple thing.

14:31.158 --> 14:32.995
Give me paw.

14:33.063 --> 14:34.734
Paw?

14:34.802 --> 14:36.807
Good.
Other paw.

14:36.874 --> 14:39.113
No. Other paw.

14:39.182 --> 14:40.652
No!
We practiced this!

14:40.720 --> 14:42.256
You're gonna make me look bad
in front of the other guys.

14:42.324 --> 14:44.060
Other paw!

14:45.432 --> 14:46.501
Finally!

14:46.569 --> 14:47.672
You know, this
actually reminds me

14:47.740 --> 14:48.975
of a quote by Milton...

14:49.043 --> 14:50.914
Shut the (bleep) up.

14:50.982 --> 14:52.619
Well, what are we gonna do?

14:52.688 --> 14:53.580
What are we
gonna do about what?

14:53.605 --> 14:54.541
(all gasp)

14:54.542 --> 14:55.711
Oh, about the...

14:55.779 --> 14:58.186
The, uh, th-th-the pie!

14:58.253 --> 15:00.124
The pie we're all
gonna make for you for...

15:00.193 --> 15:01.729
being such a great guy.

15:01.797 --> 15:03.869
Aw, my God,
that sounds awesome.

15:03.920 --> 15:05.524
I would kill everyone
in the world

15:05.591 --> 15:07.997
and leave three survivors
for a piece of pie right now.

15:08.064 --> 15:10.654
(nervous laughing)

15:12.545 --> 15:13.781
Guys, really, what
are we gonna do?

15:13.849 --> 15:15.252
Well, it seems obvious.

15:15.320 --> 15:17.827
We gotta find a way
to kill him before he kills us.

15:17.893 --> 15:19.162
Kill him?

15:19.231 --> 15:21.202
How about we just get
the hell out of here?

15:21.270 --> 15:22.841
Are you kidding me?
He'd catch us.

15:22.908 --> 15:25.482
If this guy's an alien,
I bet he can fly.

15:25.549 --> 15:27.621
He can probably
hear us right now.

15:27.689 --> 15:29.059
He's probably got a laser beam

15:29.126 --> 15:30.496
that can shoot us
through the walls.

15:30.563 --> 15:31.699
(screaming)

15:31.784 --> 15:33.321
He can't hit us
if we keep moving!

15:33.372 --> 15:35.427
Can you... Can you not...
Can you...

15:35.495 --> 15:37.550
I just took a bunch of
random stuff I found

15:37.634 --> 15:39.238
in my medicine cabinet,
and you're really

15:39.307 --> 15:40.442
freaking me out
right now.

15:40.510 --> 15:42.280
Okay, maybe he doesn't
have a laser.

15:42.348 --> 15:45.523
But listen, if we're gonna kill
him, we gotta find some guns.

15:45.591 --> 15:47.412
Okay, well, let's go.

15:47.496 --> 15:49.451
Not all of us. Somebody's
gotta go over there

15:49.519 --> 15:51.926
and keep an eye on him, make
sure he doesn't go anywhere.

15:51.993 --> 15:53.162
Oh, come on.
Why me?

15:53.230 --> 15:54.867
'Cause I'm your owner
and I said so.

15:54.935 --> 15:56.338
But I don't want to.

15:56.406 --> 15:57.608
All right, then,
you asked for it!

15:58.745 --> 16:00.149
What, what is that?

16:00.216 --> 16:01.570
I found it
in my night table.

16:01.638 --> 16:03.844
I thought it was a dog whistle,
but now I'm thinking

16:03.911 --> 16:06.367
it's something you jam in your
urethra to make you last longer.

16:11.315 --> 16:13.187
Man, I wonder if I'm one
of those secret assassins

16:13.254 --> 16:14.524
who doesn't even know it,

16:14.592 --> 16:16.430
but I'm a highly trained
killing machine.

16:16.498 --> 16:18.602
Well, I could test that
by attacking you.

16:18.670 --> 16:20.107
If you repel my attack,

16:20.174 --> 16:21.578
maybe that means
you're a secret assassin.

16:21.646 --> 16:23.182
Good idea.

16:24.688 --> 16:27.897
I don't, I don't think
I'm a secret assassin.

16:30.322 --> 16:32.062
(knocking)
Hey, uh...

16:32.063 --> 16:34.201
knock, knock,
a-anybody home?

16:34.269 --> 16:35.404
Oh, hey, buddy.
Come on in,

16:35.473 --> 16:36.909
I could use some company.

16:36.977 --> 16:38.648
Um, okay.

16:38.716 --> 16:40.537
Hey, I know we're the only
people on Earth and all,

16:40.605 --> 16:41.940
but what's with
all these Mexicans

16:42.008 --> 16:43.679
coming here
to steal our jobs?

16:43.746 --> 16:45.116
Hey, what are you
doin' down there?

16:45.184 --> 16:46.854
Come on, sit up on
the couch with me.

16:46.922 --> 16:48.827
Are you sure?

16:48.895 --> 16:51.569
Mr. Quagmire says dogs aren't
allowed on the furniture.

16:51.637 --> 16:52.972
I don't care
about that stuff.

16:53.040 --> 16:55.079
Besides, you look like
you got a clean bum.

16:55.146 --> 16:57.519
It is pretty clean.
I just cleaned it.

16:57.587 --> 16:59.458
Ha. Bums are funny.

16:59.526 --> 17:01.330
(chuckles)
They are kinda funny.

17:01.398 --> 17:02.986
We all got one.
We all got one!

17:03.053 --> 17:05.158
I was just gonna say that!
Isn't-isn't that weird?

17:05.225 --> 17:06.662
(chuckles)
Everybody's got a bum!

17:06.730 --> 17:08.568
(both laughing)

17:08.619 --> 17:10.056
Mine's even got a secret
compartment in it

17:10.124 --> 17:11.259
where you can store stuff.

17:11.343 --> 17:12.429
Hey, you want a pretzel?

17:12.497 --> 17:13.733
I'm okay.

17:13.801 --> 17:15.806
You know, you ever think
if we could all just

17:15.874 --> 17:18.279
spend more time celebrating our
similarities instead of just

17:18.347 --> 17:19.733
standing on our differences,
the universe

17:19.801 --> 17:21.205
would be a much better place?

17:21.272 --> 17:23.060
Not really.
But that bum thing,

17:23.128 --> 17:24.364
you're-you're on
to something there.

17:24.431 --> 17:25.802
Y-You're, uh...

17:25.869 --> 17:28.191
you're some kind of deep
thinker, aren't you?

17:31.000 --> 17:32.136
(tires screech)

17:33.023 --> 17:34.359
Where you goin'?

17:34.427 --> 17:35.864
I-I think your...

17:35.948 --> 17:37.552
your pie might be
about ready.

17:37.621 --> 17:39.491
Hey, we're gonna share
that pie, buddy,

17:39.559 --> 17:41.764
'cause, you know,
there's no "I" in "pie."

17:41.832 --> 17:42.693
Except for the "I."

17:42.694 --> 17:44.431
But enough about
numbers. You go.

17:47.113 --> 17:48.495
So, we ready
to do this?

17:48.496 --> 17:49.833
You guys, I'm
not sure that

17:49.901 --> 17:51.371
Peter's the guy
we think he is.

17:51.439 --> 17:54.179
He seems harmless and
actually kinda nice.

17:54.246 --> 17:55.515
Oh, my God.

17:55.583 --> 17:56.753
You slept with him!

17:56.821 --> 17:58.056
What? No, no.

17:58.125 --> 18:00.012
We were just watching TV,
but listen,

18:00.080 --> 18:02.620
you've got to believe me, he's
not capable of hurting anyone.

18:02.689 --> 18:04.558
Clearly he's
controlling your mind

18:04.626 --> 18:06.699
with his superior
alien brain.

18:06.766 --> 18:08.955
PETER: Ah, don't let 'em get
you down, Paul Blart.

18:09.022 --> 18:10.559
Your life has dignity.

18:10.627 --> 18:12.565
(laughs)
And comedy!

18:12.633 --> 18:14.505
Oh, heavens!

18:14.572 --> 18:16.476
Look, there's pretty solid
evidence that this guy

18:16.544 --> 18:18.249
is responsible
for the elimination of

18:18.316 --> 18:21.541
the entire human race,
and we need to take him out.

18:21.609 --> 18:22.962
Okay, okay, you're right.

18:23.030 --> 18:25.102
But he trusts me, so

18:25.170 --> 18:26.573
you guys wait here,

18:26.641 --> 18:27.976
and I'll go lure him out.

18:31.823 --> 18:34.730
I have a lot of
dirty stuff in my house.

18:34.798 --> 18:36.435
Wait, what the
hell's he doing?

18:39.244 --> 18:41.349
He's supposed to be
luring Peter out here.

18:41.417 --> 18:42.719
He's not doing
anything like that.

18:42.788 --> 18:43.890
He's warning him!

18:43.958 --> 18:45.294
They think I'm an alien?!

18:45.345 --> 18:47.116
Yes, and you have to get
out of here right away!

18:47.184 --> 18:48.955
But you're-you're
Quagmire's dog.

18:49.023 --> 18:50.927
Why would you be
helping me instead of him?

18:50.994 --> 18:52.298
Because...

18:52.365 --> 18:54.370
I-I don't...
I don't know why.

18:54.438 --> 18:55.473
I-I can't explain it.

18:55.541 --> 18:56.610
I-I just...

18:56.678 --> 18:59.251
I feel like
you're my friend.

18:59.320 --> 19:00.422
(sighs)
You wouldn't understand.

19:00.489 --> 19:02.862
No, I think I kinda do.

19:05.503 --> 19:06.874
Come on, buddy.
Let's go!

19:11.471 --> 19:14.178
I knew I couldn't trust you,
you filthy mongrel.

19:14.229 --> 19:15.833
Guys, he didn't
do it, I swear.

19:15.901 --> 19:17.203
Get out of the way, dog.

19:18.993 --> 19:21.165
(shouts)
Please! I didn't do anything!

19:21.232 --> 19:23.505
When you've been a stripper
as long as I have,

19:23.573 --> 19:25.678
you know when you've
met a bad egg.

19:25.746 --> 19:27.282
And you're a bad egg.

19:42.293 --> 19:44.700
No! You bastards!

19:48.446 --> 19:51.536
(sobbing)

19:51.604 --> 19:53.041
(screams)

19:53.109 --> 19:54.846
(beeping)

19:54.914 --> 19:57.053
What the hell...

19:57.121 --> 19:58.507
What's going on?

20:00.230 --> 20:01.348
Stewie?

20:01.416 --> 20:03.020
Well, Brian,
you proved me wrong.

20:03.088 --> 20:04.608
What the hell
are you talking about?

20:04.675 --> 20:06.079
What, what is all this?

20:06.147 --> 20:08.837
You see, Brian, I conducted
a little experiment.

20:08.888 --> 20:10.642
Remember our
little argument about

20:10.710 --> 20:12.515
whether you and Peter
were actually friends?

20:12.566 --> 20:14.887
Well, I wanted to prove
to you that I was right,

20:14.956 --> 20:17.829
that your friendship was purely
a result of circumstance.

20:17.897 --> 20:21.240
So I created a scenario in which
everyone's memories were erased,

20:21.307 --> 20:23.179
to demonstrate
that you and Peter

20:23.247 --> 20:25.202
would never naturally
associate with one another.

20:25.268 --> 20:26.605
But I was wrong.

20:26.673 --> 20:29.697
It appears you two have
a genuine bond after all.

20:29.765 --> 20:31.135
Wow.

20:31.203 --> 20:34.027
So we really were meant
to be friends.

20:34.095 --> 20:35.464
I guess you were, yes.

20:35.533 --> 20:37.570
So, are they gonna
remember any of this?

20:37.638 --> 20:39.509
No, I'll wipe out
their whole day.

20:39.577 --> 20:40.646
It'll be like
it never happened.

20:40.714 --> 20:41.983
Wow.

20:42.051 --> 20:43.705
Hey, what's going
on over there?

20:45.177 --> 20:47.526
Oh, I wanted to see how
three women would react

20:47.552 --> 20:48.502
in the same situation.

20:48.503 --> 20:49.755
(arguing and screaming)
Stop it!

20:49.823 --> 20:51.427
Ow! Ow!
Let go! Let go!

20:52.848 --> 20:54.799
They've only been in there
for three minutes.

20:54.800 --> 20:57.257
Haven't even tried to figure
out each other's names yet.

20:57.258 --> 21:58.258
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru